+The scoped-cycle-bit proposal is not ready for native testing as a preservation-only repair. Its fallback descendants can change even when it skips new defaulting on a cycle-touching frame. This is a concrete source-level counterexample; no browser execution or native proof was performed.
+
+Use registered A/B/C with A initial vertical-rl and B/C initial vertical-lr:
+
+    A: var(B, var(C)); B: var(A); C: var(--missing)
+    writing-mode: var(A, horizontal-tb)
+
+On recursive A reentry, the draft sets encountered_cycle and returns no primary. B fails. A then evaluates C in its fallback. C temporarily isolates the previous cycle bit; its missing-reference error is locally acyclic, so the new registered default supplies vertical-lr. Restoring the bit does not undo that changed result. A's cycle-touching success returns the raw vertical-lr substitution, although its marked substitution must be invalid and its own computed default vertical-rl. The outer resolver may later repair A's stored value, which does not itself repair an earlier ordinary-property application. The selected ordering must still be established by browser observations.
+
+The implementation owner independently found the same flaw and is preparing explicit participant marks. Required narrow control: both declaration orders of this fallback-crossing cycle, asserting A/B own initials and nonparticipant C's default, plus the outside writing-mode result. This is sufficient to exercise the newly identified branch; no additional broad framework is needed.
+
+The existing Lean model applies directly at the boundary: marked_survives_fallback requires preserved marks and a final participant check. A boolean saying some descendant encountered a cycle is neither the participant set nor a final poison check. The model does not establish the native caller ordering or resolver correspondence.
+
+Fixture review: the 32 expansion error cases have no concrete setup/oracle blocker. Missing var/env/typed attr, rejected typed attr, inherited versus reset defaults, root fallback to initial, substituted inherit/unset and invalid trailing keyword are isolated from the known logical-unit scheduling question by using a separate fixed 1lh request. The self/mutual cases use distinct initials; the successful primary excludes its unused self fallback. Fresh iframe registrations and collected-before-assertion mutation snapshots are appropriate.
+
+The four color cases must remain calibration observations. Their unconditional registration verdict in the archived trace is too strong: Properties API section 3 connects @property to equivalent registerProperty() behavior, while the latter rejects computationally dependent initials. The descriptor section alone only states a grammar requirement. Therefore current text does not conclusively establish acceptance of light-dark() as an @property initial. Conditional on admission, selecting the color from color-scheme is clear; failure of the independent initial calibration is not a pending-provider regression. The test owner agreed to correct the trace in a successor without rewriting the archive.
+
+Cached-default source boundary: inherited nonroot values are cloned from the actual inherited style; root/reset values use the existing Stylist initial cache. The cache is constructed using AllowComputationallyDependent::No and its computation flags are applied at cascade setup. That avoids the prior draft's early-context recomputation. It does not prove future support for contextual @property initials. CSS-wide inherited/reset handling retains the existing parent/cache split and INHERITS_RESET_STYLE effect. No additional concrete default-selection bug was found in this bounded read.
+
+Evidence: artifact reads f92462, da8337, eb62f4, 00d71d, 7b720d all exited 0. Searchfox lookup get_custom_property_initial_values_flags (938faf/0) found both the Stylist accessor and cascade add_flags call. The installed CLI does not support --permalink (eae614/2), so this report names symbols rather than inventing a revision URL. Current primary Properties API was reread 2026-10-27 at https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/; Values5 guard/default chain is pinned by the referenced model's SPEC-TRACE. No live source, build, browser, Git/index or epoch was touched.
