+Bounded semantic review of the participant-mark successor is clear. The v1 review remains a record of the concrete scoped-bit blocker; this report does not rewrite that finding.
+
+V3 marks the active stack suffix beginning at the reentered custom-property name. Marks survive fallback evaluation. Each marked provider takes its own invalid/default outcome on unwind, regardless of a nested substitution's success. A nonparticipant prefix or fallback provider is not marked merely because it consumed a cyclic participant. Normal custom-property application seeds and checks its own name too, preventing a root expression from applying additional operations to its own returned default.
+
+These changes close the exact source-level A=var(B,var(C)), B=var(A), C=var(missing) leak identified in review. General missing/grammar default selection still clones the parent for inherited nonroot properties or the Stylist initial cache for root/reset cases. CSS-wide selection retains its existing parent/cache and effect behavior. The unrelated cascade import reorder has been removed; that file only gains the Stylist argument at its invalidation call.
+
+The sealed expanded fixture now contains the A/B/C case in both orders, asserts each participant's own initial, checks C's nonparticipant default, and checks the outside writing-mode consumer. Its existing missing-var, root/inherit/unset and selected-cycle controls remain appropriate. The color initial-admission trace is now INCONCLUSIVE and its four calibration rows remain separately attributed; no unconditional light-dark registration claim is made.
+
+No further concrete semantic blocker was found in this bounded source/fixture review. This is permission to proceed to the already planned compile and focused comparison, not acceptance of an unbuilt repair. The stack tracks custom-property names; this review does not prove equivalence with all attribute/relative-unit cycles or the outer resolver's SCC machinery. Actual early application, stored values, inheritance mutations and existing cycle regressions need the planned browser evidence. The Lean model supplies a normalized participant/default invariant, not extracted Rust verification.
+
+Read evidence: V3 substantive delta 7576eb/0; final incidental-import removal b84215/0; expanded fixture delta 984032/0. Final source/fixture references below bind the sealed packages. No native, browser, build, Git/index or epoch mutation was performed.
